ation)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045437 :db/ident :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-low}] [{:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — max reasoning effort (Codex configuration)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045438 :db/ident :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-max}] [{:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — medium reasoning effort (Codex configuration)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045439 :db/ident :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-medium}] [{:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — ultra reasoning effort (Codex configuration)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045440 :db/ident :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-ultra}] [{:db/doc "GPT-6.1 Sol — xhigh reasoning effort (Codex configuration)." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045441 :db/ident :agent/gpt-6.1-sol-xhigh}] [{:db/doc "ChatGPT 6 Pro — course-map author identified from Jake's recollection; exact model not recorded in the saved export." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045442 :db/ident :agent/chatgpt-6-pro}] [{:db/doc "Course Academy engine." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045443 :db/ident :application/ca-engine}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, title, and at least one course ref when explicitly ensured. Nonempty titles and reference target types require application validation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045444 :db/ident :course-group/validate :db.entity/attrs [:course-group/courses :course-group/id :course-group/title]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, index, and outcome text when explicitly ensured. Category is optional. Nonempty text and category labels, positive indexes, index uniqueness within the course, and ownership by exactly one course require additional validation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045445 :db/ident :course-outcome/validate :db.entity/attrs [:course-outcome/id :course-outcome/index :course-outcome/text]}] [{:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder course when explicitly ensured. Use course/validate after filling in its required data." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045446 :db/ident :course/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:course/id]}] [{:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one unit ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier, course code, school, description, overview, outcomes, and next courses are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, outcome indexes unique within this course, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045447 :db/ident :course/validate :db.entity/attrs [:course/id :course/title :course/units]}] [{:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder unit when explicitly ensured. Use unit/validate after filling in its required data." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045448 :db/ident :unit/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:unit/id]}] [{:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one module ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier and next units are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation. Referenced modules must be validated separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045449 :db/ident :unit/validate :db.entity/attrs [:unit/id :unit/modules :unit/title]}] [{:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder module when explicitly ensured. Use module/validate after filling in its required data." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045450 :db/ident :module/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:module/id]}] [{:db/doc "Requires our identity, a title, and at least one topic ref when explicitly ensured. The Math Academy identifier and next modules are optional. Nonempty titles, reference target types, and prevention of self-links and cycles require application validation. Referenced topics must be validated separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045451 :db/ident :module/validate :db.entity/attrs [:module/id :module/title :module/topics]}] [{:db/doc "A curricular topic, shared across courses and containing knowledge points. Explicit db/ensure requires identity, title, and at least one knowledge-point reference. The predicate checks difficulty when present. Referenced knowledge points and encompassing records must be validated separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045452 :db/ident :topic/validate :db.entity/attrs [:topic/id :topic/knowledge-points :topic/title] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.topic/valid-difficulty?]}] [{:db/doc "Requires a component topic and weight when explicitly ensured. A valid topic target, finite weight in [0,1], and relationship consistency require additional validation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045453 :db/ident :encompassing/validate :db.entity/attrs [:encompassing/topic :encompassing/weight]}] [{:db/doc "Requires a topic identity and a strictly positive finite workload multiplier. Does not require a fully populated curriculum topic." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045454 :db/ident :topic/difficulty-validate :db.entity/attrs [:topic/difficulty :topic/id] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.topic/valid-difficulty?]}] [{:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder topic when explicitly ensured. Use topic/validate after filling in its required data." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045455 :db/ident :topic/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:topic/id]}] [{:db/doc "Native EDB specification requiring KP identity, title, a canonical example question ref, and at least one practice question ref when explicitly ensured. Writers ensure question/validate for both examples and practice questions, along with child specifications. The application checks target types, nonempty canonical worked solutions, disjointness of all canonical targets from every practice pool, mathematical correctness, and selection rules." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045456 :db/ident :knowledge-point/validate :db.entity/attrs [:knowledge-point/canonical-example :knowledge-point/id :knowledge-point/questions :knowledge-point/title]}] [{:db/doc "Requires only identity for a placeholder knowledge point when explicitly ensured. Use knowledge-point/validate after filling in its required data." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045457 :db/ident :knowledge-point/identity-validate :db.entity/attrs [:knowledge-point/id]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, title, type, steps, and an entry point. The application checks enum values, step ownership and routing, positive finite timings, and type-specific requirements: topic scope for lessons/reviews and curriculum scope for diagnostics. Assignment deadlines are optional." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045459 :db/ident :activity/validate :db.entity/attrs [:activity/first-step :activity/id :activity/steps :activity/title :activity/type]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045461 :db/ident :activity.type/assignment}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity and content when explicitly ensured. The application checks exactly one owner through activity/steps or multistep/steps, reference targets, positive finite timings, and valid continuation links. Containment must be acyclic. Validate content separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045470 :db/ident :step/validate :db.entity/attrs [:step/content :step/id]}] [{:db/doc "Native EDB specification requiring identity, title, and instructional content when explicitly ensured. Nonempty content, valid assets, and mathematical correctness require additional validation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045480 :db/ident :tutorial/validate :db.entity/attrs [:tutorial/content :tutorial/id :tutorial/title]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity and problem when explicitly ensured. The application requires complete answer fields before automatic grading, and a worked solution for canonical examples, validates any present fields and answer values, and derives example roles from knowledge-point/canonical-example and excludes those targets from every practice pool. A fieldless school problem may be displayed through assigned-problem without grading or awarding mastery." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045484 :db/ident :question/validate :db.entity/attrs [:question/id :question/problem]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, key, and type when explicitly ensured. The type-specific predicate validates owned answer values and canonical membership. Radio, select, blank, and checkbox require a nonempty bank and one canonical answer. Free permits an empty bank and no reference answer. Checkbox banks contain exactly two text answers, true and false. Writers also ensure answer/validate. Question field-key uniqueness, immutable referenced values, entered-answer reuse, and response completeness require application handling." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045491 :db/ident :answer-field/validate :db.entity/attrs [:answer-field/id :answer-field/key :answer-field/type] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.answer-field/valid?]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, type, and a string value when explicitly ensured. The application checks supported answer types and field-scoped deduplication, keeps referenced values immutable, and may validate authored image availability. Do not reject an entered value solely because its math syntax is malformed." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045496 :db/ident :answer/validate :db.entity/attrs [:answer/id :answer/type :answer/value]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, steps, and an entry point. The application checks single step ownership, a connected acyclic sibling sequence, and acyclic content nesting. Validate steps and their content separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045500 :db/ident :multistep/validate :db.entity/attrs [:multistep/first-step :multistep/id :multistep/steps]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity and content when explicitly ensured. Coverage may be added later. The application checks that content references a question or multistep and coverage references topics; validate the referenced content separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045504 :db/ident :assigned-problem/validate :db.entity/attrs [:assigned-problem/content :assigned-problem/id]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity and all FIRe retention settings. The registered predicate checks the update-order enum, finite numeric ranges, and relationships between those settings. Optional question-selection records require their own validation; the application checks their ownership and unique activity types. Formulas and applying changed settings to existing progress belong to application code." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045507 :db/ident :policy/validate :db.entity/attrs [:policy/accuracy-update-rate :policy/base-half-life-days :policy/early-practice-discount-power :policy/future-horizon-days :policy/gate-slow-implicit :policy/id :policy/initial-accuracy :policy/initial-retention :policy/interval-growth :policy/maximum-failure-multiplier :policy/maximum-half-life-days :policy/maximum-speed :policy/minimum-speed :policy/overdue-failure-slope :policy/retention-update-order :policy/review-threshold :policy/speed-exponent] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.policy/valid?]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045508 :db/ident :policy.retention-update/add-before-decay}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045509 :db/ident :policy.retention-update/decay-before-add}] [{:db/doc "Requires an activity type and all six weights when explicitly ensured. The application supports lessons, reviews, and assessments and checks finite nonnegative weights, a positive finite total for each distribution, exactly one policy owner, and one record per activity type in that policy. Lessons and reviews choose the phase using their stopping rules; ordinary assessments use initial weights throughout, while a designated assessment retake/recheck explicitly requests remedial weights. Weights are normalized across eligible bands before selecting a fresh question within the chosen band; an unavailable question supply is not learner failure. Stopping rules and retake scheduling remain application code." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045526 :db/ident :question-weights/validate :db.entity/attrs [:question-weights/activity-type :question-weights/initial-easy :question-weights/initial-hard :question-weights/initial-moderate :question-weights/remedial-easy :question-weights/remedial-hard :question-weights/remedial-moderate]}] [{:db/doc "Completed lesson: if p < 0.50, XP = -1; else if p = 1, XP = R(1.25 B); else XP = R(B min(1, 1.5 p - 0.30)). Use all ordinary question occurrences across the task, not average per-KP accuracy. A failed completed task still receives this formula's award; unfinished tasks receive no final award." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045533 :db/ident :xp-weights/lesson-v1}] [{:db/doc "Completed multistep activity: XP = max(-1, R(B (2.25 p - 1))). Count ordinary question occurrences once regardless of answer-field count. Perfect work earns R(1.25 B). The negative floor applies after rounding." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045534 :db/ident :xp-weights/multistep-v1}] [{:db/doc "Completed or expired quiz/assessment: p < 0.20 -> -1; otherwise max(0, R(1.20 B (p - 0.35) / 0.65)). N is the full assigned question count; C counts correct submissions. Unanswered questions receive no correct credit. Perfect work earns R(1.20 B). Diagnostic placement is a separate policy and does not use this rule." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045535 :db/ident :xp-weights/assessment-v1}] [{:db/doc "Completed review, in order: p < 0.50 -> -1; p = 1 -> B + 2; p >= 2/3 -> B; otherwise final ordinary question incorrect/skipped -> 0; otherwise R(B p). The final outcome must be known in the partial-credit band. The perfect bonus is additive two XP, not a percentage." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045536 :db/ident :xp-weights/review-v1}] [{:db/doc "Learner identity and knowledge-profile ownership/uniqueness. Overall performance is optional and its child record must be separately ensured with performance/validate. This spec does not validate performance ownership or values." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045537 :db/ident :learner/validate :db.entity/attrs [:learner/id] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.progress/valid-profile?]}] [{:db/doc "Requires all four values for the complete overall performance estimate. Effective accuracy is the mean of the two accuracy fields; do not persist another independently mutable copy. The writer checks exactly one learner owner, finite accuracy in [0,1], and finite nonnegative evidence mass. Update the existing child through learner/performance rather than replacing it for each observation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045538 :db/ident :performance/validate :db.entity/attrs [:performance/assessment-accuracy :performance/assessment-mass :performance/practice-accuracy :performance/practice-mass]}] [{:db/doc "Requires one learner owner, one record per topic in that profile, and complete operational state. Ability can exist while learned=false, including after failed initial lessons. Effective accuracy is the mean of the two accuracy strata. Initialization values are explicit local choices, not inferred from XP." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045547 :db/ident :progress/validate :db.entity/attrs [:progress/assessment-accuracy :progress/assessment-mass :progress/id :progress/interval-days :progress/learned :progress/memory :progress/memory-at :progress/policy :progress/practice-accuracy :progress/practice-mass :progress/repetitions :progress/topic] :db.entity/preds [course-academy.progress/valid-progress?]}] [{:db/doc "Requires identity, activity, and lifecycle state. The application checks one learner association, valid content, enums, and timing; validate child records separately." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045562 :db/ident :learner-task/validate :db.entity/attrs [:learner-task/activity :learner-task/id :learner-task/status]}] [{:db/doc "Requires presentation identity and status. The next link is optional; historical content may be unknown. Task membership, chain consistency, status transitions, and derived elapsed totals require application validation." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186045563 :db/ident :task-item/validate :db.entity/attrs [:task-item/id :task-item/status]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045564 :db/ident :learner-task.status/completed}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045565 :db/ident :learner-task.status/failed}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045566 :db/ident :learner-task.status/locked}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045567 :db/ident :learner-task.status/paused}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045568 :db/ident :learner-task.status/started}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045569 :db/ident :learner-task.status/unlocked}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045570 :db/ident :task-item.status/completed}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571 :db/ident :task-item.status/correct}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045572 :db/ident :task-item.status/incorrect}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045573 :db/ident :task-item.status/paused}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045574 :db/ident :task-item.status/skipped}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045575 :db/ident :task-item.status/started}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408167 :db/ident :answer-field.type/free}]}
